[TPU/CI] Fix upstream sync regressions, premature device initialization, and test suites

- Mem Cache & Hardware Backend:
  * Defer get_device_module() evaluation in l2_transfer.py to avoid premature PjRt runtime initialization during module imports.
  * Guard get_device_total_memory() in tpu_platform.py against uninitialized backend states.
  * Update get_req_to_token_extra_context_len call signature in attention_pallas_rpa_base.py.

- Disaggregation & Prefill/Decode:
  * Skip prompt tensor flattening and device copy in prepare_for_prebuilt() (ScheduleBatchDisaggregationDecodeMixin), setting input_ids = None.
  * Remove unused server_args parameter in process_prebuilt() and build_disagg_draft_input() to align with upstream SpeculativeAlgorithm.
  * Restore upstream deferred KV release, staging handler, BlockStoredMetadata in kv_events.py, and multimodal helpers in encode_receiver.py / encode_server.py.
  * Increase socket receive timeout in test_disagg_tpu_transfer.py for TPU CI stability.

- Tests & CI Registrations:
  * In test_prefix_cache.py (test_tpu_qwen3_0_6b_singlehost_prefix_cache.py), adjust CHURN loop to keep prompt lengths safely within the model context length (1024).
  * In test_distributed_top_k_sampling.py, skip TP8 physical collective speed benchmarks when fewer than 8 TPU devices are available.
  * Align configuration ratchets (test_supplied_instance_exposure_ratchet, test_global_config_read_ratchet, test_decode_kvcache_offload_manager).
  * Standardize test class names and CustomTestCase inheritance across e2e and unit test suites.
